{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"b723ad4b-041a-4b34-81b4-19c48a5dd259","agentId":"a3d9a94747dce8021","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Do not spawn subagents or forks. Do not commit or push. Be token-efficient. Do not edit cuore/app.py, anything under cuore/web/ (another agent owns the page), or mes-log-mcp/. NEVER add an HTTP route that writes to the car (no clear, actuate, routine, session-control, Mode 04): that is a hard project rule.\n\nContext: repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers; cuore = FastAPI app (cuore/), Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe; tests set CUORE_STATE_DIR to a temp dir before importing cuore. The HTTP API (117 operations, see create_app().openapi()) is grouped by developer tags; a mechanic cannot use it. Build the data side of a mechanic-facing Tools catalogue that a page agent renders at /tools against EXACTLY this contract.\n\n1. cuore/services/tools_bridge.py:\n- `catalogue(app_openapi: dict, state: dict) -> dict` returning {\"groups\": [{\"id\", \"title\", \"blurb\", \"tools\": [tool...]}], \"workflows\": [...], \"state\": {...}, \"coverage\": {\"total_operations\": n, \"curated\": n, \"developer_only\": n}}.\n- tool = {\"id\": \"<method> <path>\", \"method\", \"path\", \"name\" (plain words), \"what\" (what it tells you, one sentence), \"when\" (when to use it), \"needs\": [\"car\"|\"cable\"|\"vin\"|\"mes_stopped\"|\"live_session\"|\"module\"], \"risk\": \"reads_car\"|\"reads_logs\"|\"writes_cuore_state\"|\"holds_adapter\", \"inputs\": [{\"name\", \"in\": \"path\"|\"query\"|\"body\", \"label\", \"type\", \"required\", \"default\", \"source\": \"active_vin\"|\"cable\"|\"port\"|\"vehicle_modules\"|\"live_channels\"|\"recent_codes\"|None, \"choices\": [...]|None, \"help\"}], \"run\": \"one_tap\"|\"form\"|\"not_from_here\", \"enabled\": bool, \"disabled_reason\": str|None, \"result_hint\": \"table\"|\"codes\"|\"readiness\"|\"text\"|\"raw\", \"developer_only\": bool, \"synonyms\": [plain words]}.\n- Curated overlay: a Python table keyed by (method, path) with name/what/when/needs/risk/inputs sources/synonyms for EVERY operation that a mechanic could use; developer-only ones (openapi, learn/correlate internals, layouts CRUD, etc.) get developer_only=True and are still listed from the spec with the summary as name. Add a self-check: every operation in the spec is either curated or marked developer_only (test asserts this), so a new route can never be silently missing.\n- Groups (in this order): \"read_car\" Read the car now; \"verify\" Check a repair; \"history\" History and logs; \"live\" Live data and recording; \"service\" Service and maintenance; \"learn\" Learning and dealer results; \"settings\" Adapter and settings; \"developer\" For developers (collapsed).\n- Also list, in group \"writes\", the MCP-only operations that are deliberately NOT in HTTP (clear_module_dtcs, run_actuator, routines) as cards with run=\"not_from_here\", the exact consent phrase format (CLEAR <MODULE>, ACTUATE <MODULE> <NAME>, RUN ROUTINE <MODULE> <NAME>) and the blocked-module list from cuore/live/safety.py; read it, do not duplicate constants.\n- `state` comes from `current_state()`: active VIN (cookie value is passed in by the page), live status via cuore.live.ops.status() (port, mes_state, cable, buses verified, lock holder, poller holds adapter), the car's logged ECUs for that VIN (mes_bridge.workup identity) and whether the adapter port exists. Enablement rules: needs \"car\" -> port present and MES not connected and no other lock holder; \"live_session\" -> poller active; \"mes_stopped\" -> mes_state != connected; \"vin\" -> active VIN set; \"cable\" -> cable declared. disabled_reason in plain words (\"Connect the car: no adapter on COM3\", \"Close MultiEcuScan first: it holds the port\").\n- `suggest(state, catalogue) -> [tool ids]`: next sensible tools (e.g. no cable declared -> set cable; car connected and no bus verified -> verify bus; codes read but no readiness -> readiness; verdict UNVERIFIED -> verify repair).\n- Workflows (semi-automatic, read-only): {\"id\", \"title\", \"blurb\", \"steps\": [{\"tool_id\", \"label\", \"stop_on_fail\": bool, \"uses_previous\": str|None}]}: \"check_car\" (probe -> cable check -> verify can_c -> OBD codes stored+pending+permanent -> readiness -> freeze frame -> UDS scan of confirmed modules), \"verify_repair\" (readiness -> permanent -> dossier verify), \"prep_live\" (probe -> verify -> live channels list). Only reads.\n2. cuore/api/tools.py router: GET /tools/catalogue (query vin optional), GET /tools/suggest, GET /tools/workflows. Report the include line (prefix /api).\n3. Result shaping for the page: `shape_result(tool_id, payload) -> {\"kind\": \"table\"|\"codes\"|\"readiness\"|\"kv\"|\"text\", \"title\", \"columns\"|None, \"rows\"|None, \"summary\": one plain sentence}` with shapers for: DTC reads (code, description if known, status words from status byte bits 0x01/0x04/0x08/0x80), readiness (monitor, complete/incomplete, EVAP verdict), module identity, voltage, status, workup/dossier summaries, lists of logs/recordings; generic kv/table fallback. Expose POST /api/tools/shape {tool_id, payload} for the page.\n4. Tests cuore/tests/check_tools.py: every spec operation curated or developer_only; no tool in the catalogue has method POST/PUT/DELETE with risk reads_car that would write (assert the HTTP catalogue contains none of the write operations; grep the spec for clear/actuat/routine paths and assert absent); enablement: with a fake state (no port) every needs-car tool is disabled with a reason; with port + mes stopped they enable; suggest() ordering cases; shape_result on a sample DTC payload yields readable status words; coverage numbers consistent. Run it plus cuore/tests/check_api.py and check_live.py.\nReport: files, include line, counts (curated / developer_only), test results, and the JSON of two example tools (read codes, readiness)."},"uuid":"bddf34ec-4364-4119-81c4-38056ce9a0fd","timestamp":"2026-10-08T01:20:14.786Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
